### Rotating Card (Hover Effect)

Below is a minimal, self‑contained example that shows a card flipping around the Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy the code into an `.html` file and open it in a browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
/* 1️⃣  Container – gives the 3D space */
.card {
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  perspective: 1000px;          /* Creates depth */
  margin: 50px auto;            /* Center horizontally */
}

/* 2️⃣  Inner wrapper – holds front & back */
.card-inner {
  position: relative;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  text-align: center;
  transition: transform 0.8s;   /* Smooth animation */
  transform-style: preserve-3d; /* Needed for 3D children */
}

/* 3️⃣  Front side */
.card-front, .card-back {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden;  /* Hide backside when rotated */
  border-radius: 10px;
  box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  color: #fff;
}

/* Front styling */
.card-front {
  background: #3498db;          /* Blue */
}

/* Back styling */
.card-back {
  background: #e74c3c;          /* Red */
  transform: rotateY(180deg);   /* Start flipped */
}

/* 4️⃣  Hover effect – flip the card */
.card:hover .card-inner {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card">
  <div class="card-inner">
    <div class="card-front">
      Front
    </div>
    <div class="card-back">
      Back
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

#### How it works

| Step | What happens |
|------|--------------|
| **1** | `perspective` on the container creates a 3D environment. |
| **2** | `transform-style: preserve-3d` keeps child elements in 3D space. |
| **3** | `backface-visibility: hidden` hides the backside when it’s turned away from the viewer. |
| **4** | On hover, the inner wrapper rotates 180° around the Y‑axis, revealing the back side. |

#### Customization tips

- **Change rotation axis**: Replace `rotateY(180deg)` with `rotateX(180deg)` for a vertical flip.
- **Add more content**: Put images, text, or other elements inside `.card-front` and `.card-back`.
- **Adjust speed**: Modify `transition: transform 0.8s;` to make the flip faster or slower.
- **Add shadows or borders**: Enhance visual depth with CSS shadows or borders.

Enjoy experimenting with this rotating card!
